init (wasm): pin the running pnpm, not the registry's latest (homescoop)

`pnpm init` pins a new project to the registry's `latest` pnpm
(devEngines.packageManager with onFail: download, and packageManager).
Native pnpm then downloads that version on the next command. A
WebContainer pnpm can't install or switch to another pnpm, so every
later command in the new project failed with ERR_PNPM_UNSUPPORTED_RUNTIME
("cannot install or switch to pnpm v12.14.0") as soon as `latest` moved
past the build: `pnpm init && pnpm add is-odd` failed in slicc on
12.9.1-13. On wasm, version_to_pin answers the running version, as it
already does offline.

Upstream: not filed (Lars decides).
removeWhen: upstream's wasm build pins the running version in `pnpm init`.

